### Welcome to SEDS Ocean

SEDS Ocean is the specialized student chapter at the Ocean University of Sri Lanka (OCUSL). Operating at the nexus of space technology and marine sciences, our chapter brings together undergraduates studying marine engineering, oceanography, fisheries, and nautical sciences.

SEDS Ocean investigates how orbital satellites, remote sensing sensors, and aerospace telemetry can protect marine ecosystems and advance oceanic research around the island of Sri Lanka.

### Focus Areas and Student Activities

SEDS Ocean bridges aerospace engineering and ocean sciences through practical projects:

- **Marine Satellite Remote Sensing**: Processing satellite altimetry, ocean color imagery (Chlorophyll-a concentrations), and sea surface temperature (SST) data from open NASA and Copernicus Earth observation satellites.
- **Coastal Telemetry and Sensor Buoys**: Designing DIY floating sensor pods equipped with GPS, water temperature sensors, and LoRa transceivers to transmit coastal ocean data.
- **Amateur Weather and Marine Satellite Reception**: Setting up ground radio receivers to decode live weather maps and sea storm telemetry from passing polar-orbiting satellites.
- **Marine STEM Outreach**: Visiting coastal communities and schools to raise awareness of how space satellites help fishermen, monitor monsoon patterns, and conserve coral reefs.

### Join SEDS Ocean

Membership is open to all students at the Ocean University of Sri Lanka.

- **Main Campus**: Ocean University of Sri Lanka, Crow Island, Colombo 15.
- **Email**: [sedsocean@sedssl.org](mailto:sedsocean@sedssl.org)
- **Membership**: Free for all enrolled undergraduates.
